      "line_number": 34,
      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "SQL query built from request input",
      "description": "Search uses fmt.Sprintf to put the name query parameter straight into the SQL text. No escaping or binding happens first. Any client can inject SQL through the name parameter. The attacker can then read or change any row the database user can reach. Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter. Remove the formatted string.",
      "suggested_change": "rows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search uses fmt.Sprintf to put the name query parameter straight into the SQL text. No escaping or binding happens first.",
      "consequence": "Any client can inject SQL through the name parameter. The attacker can then read or change any row the database user can reach.",
      "fix": "Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter. Remove the formatted string."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 63,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex left locked on missing key",
      "description": "Count locks h.mu before it checks the key. The empty-key branch then returns without unlocking h.mu. One request without a key leaves h.mu locked for good. Every later /count request then blocks forever. Validate the key before calling h.mu.Lock. Another option is to defer h.mu.Unlock right after the lock.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count locks h.mu before it checks the key. The empty-key branch then returns without unlocking h.mu.",
      "consequence": "One request without a key leaves h.mu locked for good. Every later /count request then blocks forever.",
      "fix": "Validate the key before calling h.mu.Lock. Another option is to defer h.mu.Unlock right after the lock."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 83,
      "title": "Response body closed before error check",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil, so the deferred call dereferences nil. Each unreachable upstream panics fetchStatus. The server then aborts the connection instead of sending the intended 502. Move the defer below the err check.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil, so the deferred call dereferences nil.",
      "consequence": "Each unreachable upstream panics fetchStatus. The server then aborts the connection instead of sending the intended 502.",
      "fix": "Move the defer below the err check."
    },
